  "decision_conditions": [
    "The development hereby permitted must be begun not later than the end of three years from the date of this permission. \r\rReason: To comply with the provisions of S.51 of the Planning & Compulsory Purchase Act 2004.\r",
    "The development hereby permitted shall be carried out in accordance with the following approved plans: \r\rLocation Plan; Block Plan; 3595/7 (received 18.05.2026); highway impact assessment; Energy statement by Vision Energy dated 03/02/2026; water efficiency calculations by Vision Energy (Reference: 06514).\r\rReason: For the avoidance of doubt and in the interests of proper planning. \r",
    "Notwithstanding the submitted drawings, prior to first occupation of the development hereby permitted, cycle parking must be provided in compliance with the following criteria, unless otherwise submitted to and approved in writing by the Local Planning Authority:\ro\tProvision of a minimum of THREE long stay cycle parking spaces\ro\tin an accessible location: the access route to the store should be a minimum of 1.2m wide to enable the bike to enter the store, should be step free and involve no more than 2 doors or gates (excluding the store door) which must also have a minimum opening width of 1.2m\ro\tsecured: with a British Standard mortice lock or access fob\ro\tfully enclosed: 4 walls and a roof\rReason: The Council's Climate Action and Transport Policies seek to increase the use of active and sustainable transport modes. This means that access to bicycle parking should be easy and secure to remove potential barriers to cycling.\r",
    "Notwithstanding the submitted drawings, prior to first occupation of the development hereby permitted,  refuse storage facilities, including facilities for the recycling of waste to satisfy the future number of occupiers on site, shall be provided within the development, in accordance with the London Borough of Enfield - Waste and Recycling Planning Storage Guidance ENV 08/162.\r\rReason: In order to facilitate efficient, safe and clean removal of household refuse, the location and accessibility of refuse storage plus to maintain safety on the Highway.\r\r",
    "The development shall be carried out in accordance with the submitted Energy Statement prepared Vision Energy dated 03/02/2026. All approved energy efficiency and low-carbon measures shall be installed before first occupation and retained thereafter for the lifetime of the development.\r\rReason: In the interest of sustainable development and to ensure that the Local Planning Authority may be satisfied that CO2 emission reduction targets are met in accordance with Policy CP20 of the Enfield Core Strategy (2010), Policies DMD49, DMD50 and DMD51 of the Enfield Development Management Document (2014).\r"
  ],
